Unreleased:
  detect WebRTC support via Home Assistant camera/capabilities websocket command with state attribute fallback

0.4.0-alpha.5:
  add pseudo-fullscreen view mode for stream playback with overlay controls
  support container-level fullscreen preserving lights, locks, and glance icons
  add iOS Safari-friendly viewport pseudo-fullscreen fallback
  cleanly exit fullscreen on stream stop, recording stop, or video end
  support Escape key to exit pseudo-fullscreen mode
  update localization strings for fullscreen toggle
  fix door2 status strings to use door_open and door_closed language lookups
  add dynamic entity resolution supporting modern and legacy aarlo entity naming
  auto-detect camera spotlight and doorbell ding entities when omitted from card config

0.4.0-alpha.4:
  add native Home Assistant WebRTC live streaming support with automatic capability detection
  support webrtc / sip in image_view options
  coordinate clean stream teardown when playing library recordings
  cleanly destroy WebRTC peer connections and release media on element disconnect
  document WebRTC features and add release notes for v0.4.0-alpha.4

0.4.0-alpha.3:
  generalize visual editor labels for locks and lights (remove location-specific wording)
  split widget configuration into left and right chip selectors in visual editor
  modularize project architecture into src/ with dedicated view components
  integrate Rollup build pipeline with fast watch mode (npm run watch)
  generate external sourcemaps (dist/hass-aarlo.js.map)
  add GitHub Actions CI/CD workflows for HACS validation and release asset builds
  adopt SemVer hyphen formatting (0.4.0-alpha.3)
